<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi all,<br>I'm having some troubles with the volume knob, and I'd like to ask you if anyone faced anything similar.<br>Once I turn the radio on rotating the knob, it shuts down as soon as I go a little further (as everybody would do to increase the volume); at this point, if I decrease the volume turning the knob, it turns on again.<br>It seems like it likes to be "on" only if the knob is "right after" the click: as soon as I deviate from this position, the radio goes off.<br><br>This behaviour is not deterministic: sometimes it happens as soon as I keep the transceiver in my hands, and no matter how many times I try to turn it on and off. Sometimes it behaves normally for 20 minutes, 1 hour and then starts behaving like that. <br><br>Is it cursed ?</div></blockquote>Hi Matteo,<br><br>As per your explanation it looks like a electro-mechanical issue in the switch.<br><br>I may suggest you to:<br>-Check PCB soldering related to the knob. By check I mean, redo 'cause they may look like ok and not being working properly.<br>-Softly lateral press (not turning, not down) to check whether it goes off or not. If it goes off at any moment... Knob needs to be replaced.<br><br>Suggestions based on my own experience at electronics' service shop (car radio used to behave that way...)<br><br>I hope this helps.<br><br>P.D.:<br>As far as I see, it is nothing related to FW nor Codeplug, it's pure <em class="text-italics">electronics</em> item.<br><br>P.D.2:<br>If needed, you can find replacement knob in here:<br>If my memories are not wrong, you need 10K ohm with switch.<br><a href="https://a.aliexpress.com/_ExdSkMF" class="postlink">https://a.aliexpress.com/_ExdSkMF</a> or...<br><a href="https://a.aliexpress.com/_EyJWR8P" class="postlink">https://a.aliexpress.com/_EyJWR8P</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=101">EA3FA</a> — Wed Aug 30, 2023 6:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
